#: src/scraped-examples.md:1
msgid "Scraped examples"
msgstr ""

#: src/scraped-examples.md:3
msgid ""
"Rustdoc has an unstable feature where it can automatically scrape examples "
"of items being documented from the `examples/` directory of a Cargo "
"workspace. These examples will be included within the generated "
"documentation for that item. For example, if your library contains a public "
"function:"
msgstr ""

#: src/scraped-examples.md:6
msgid "// a_crate/src/lib.rs\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/scraped-examples.md:10
msgid "And you have an example calling this function:"
msgstr ""

#: src/scraped-examples.md:13
msgid "// a_crate/examples/ex.rs\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/scraped-examples.md:19
msgid ""
"Then this code snippet will be included in the documentation for `a_func`. "
"This documentation is inserted by Rustdoc and cannot be manually edited by "
"the crate author."
msgstr ""

#: src/scraped-examples.md:22
msgid "How to use this feature"
msgstr ""

#: src/scraped-examples.md:24
msgid ""
"This feature is unstable, so you can enable it by calling Rustdoc with the "
"unstable `rustdoc-scrape-examples` flag:"
msgstr ""

#: src/scraped-examples.md:30
msgid ""
"To enable this feature on [docs.rs](https://docs.rs), add this to your Cargo."
"toml:"
msgstr ""

#: src/scraped-examples.md:32
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[package.metadata.docs.rs]\n"
"cargo-args = [\"-Zunstable-options\", \"-Zrustdoc-scrape-examples\"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/scraped-examples.md:38
msgid "How it works"
msgstr ""

#: src/scraped-examples.md:40
msgid ""
"When you run `cargo doc`, Rustdoc will analyze all the crates that match "
"Cargo's `--examples` filter for instances of items being documented. Then "
"Rustdoc will include the source code of these instances in the generated "
"documentation."
msgstr ""

#: src/scraped-examples.md:42
msgid ""
"Rustdoc has a few techniques to ensure these examples don't overwhelm "
"documentation readers, and that it doesn't blow up the page size:"
msgstr ""

#: src/scraped-examples.md:44
msgid ""
"For a given item, a maximum of 5 examples are included in the page. The "
"remaining examples are just links to source code."
msgstr ""

#: src/scraped-examples.md:45
msgid ""
"Only one example is shown by default, and the remaining examples are hidden "
"behind a toggle."
msgstr ""

#: src/scraped-examples.md:46
msgid ""
"For a given file that contains examples, only the item containing the "
"examples will be included in the generated documentation."
msgstr ""

#: src/scraped-examples.md:48
msgid ""
"For a given item, Rustdoc sorts its examples based on the size of the "
"example — smaller ones are shown first."
msgstr ""

#: src/scraped-examples.md:51
msgid "FAQ"
msgstr ""

#: src/scraped-examples.md:53
msgid "My example is not showing up in the documentation"
msgstr ""

#: src/scraped-examples.md:55
msgid ""
"This feature uses Cargo's convention for finding examples. You should ensure "
"that `cargo check --examples` includes your example file."
msgstr ""
